# What `vercel --prod` must never upload.
#
# The Vercel CLI deploys the WORKING DIRECTORY, not the git HEAD — so a file
# being untracked or .gitignore'd does not keep it out of a deploy once this
# file exists (.vercelignore takes over from .gitignore the moment it is
# present). Everything that must stay off the deployment is therefore listed
# here explicitly, not just in .gitignore.

# ── Never upload ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel skips these by default, but .vercelignore replaces .gitignore as the
# rule source, so they are restated rather than assumed.
node_modules
.next
.git

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.claude/
.vercel/

# ── Local scratch / debug scripts ───────────────────────────
# These read SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY and may embed test credentials.
_tmp_*
*.local.mjs
scripts/
hf-admin/
hf-teacher/
load-tests/
backups/

# ── Agent + capture scratch output ──────────────────────────
# Anything under public/ is served at the site root, so scratch output there
# is published. public/capture-admin/ held internal agent instruction files
# and admin-UI screenshots and would have been live at /capture-admin/*.
public/capture-admin/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.cursorrules

# ── Internal audit + planning docs ──────────────────────────
# These describe the security model, known gaps and remediation state. They
# are not served by Next.js, but there is no reason to ship them at all.
*_AUDIT.md
*_REPORT.md
*_PLAN.md
SECURITY*.md
SECRETS.md
API_SECURITY_MATRIX.md
ARCHITECTURE_AND_HARDENING_AUDIT.md
DESIGN_*.md
PRODUCT_COMPLETENESS_AUDIT.md
ROUTE_QA_REPORT.md
FIXES_FOR_SONNET.md
DEPLOYMENT.md
docs/

# ── Database migrations ─────────────────────────────────────
# Applied by hand in the Supabase SQL Editor; the running app never reads
# them. Shipping them publishes the full schema and RLS policy source.
supabase/

# ── Tests + build artefacts ─────────────────────────────────
src/__tests__/
tests/
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright.config.ts
vitest.config.ts
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.github/
